  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #06b6d422; color: #06b6d4; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">06</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Step 6</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">You will be provided with a copy of the new RC, which should be kept with you for future reference.</p>
  </div>
</div>

2. Form 30 Application:
Form 30, also known as the "Application for Temporary Licence," is required when transporting a vehicle temporarily from one state to another in India. This form ensures that the vehicle can be temporarily used while awaiting the issuance of the new registration certificate (RC) in the new state. Here's a brief overview of the process:

   <ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
       <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Step 1: Obtain a copy of the vehicle's registration certificate (RC) from the old RTO office.</span></li>
       <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Step 2: Visit the new RTO office in the state where you are relocating to.</span></li>
       <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Step 3: Submit the Form 30 along with the vehicle's registration certificate (RC) and the original RC to the new RTO office.</span></li>
       <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Step 4: The RTO will review your application and may request additional documents or information.</span></li>
       <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Step 5: After reviewing your application, the RTO will issue a temporary license (Temporary Registration Certificate - TRC) for the vehicle.</span></li>
       <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Step 6: You will be provided with a copy of the TRC, which will allow you to temporarily use the vehicle in the new state.</span></li>
       <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Step 7: Once the new registration certificate (RC) is issued by the new RTO, surrender the TRC along with the old RC.</span></li>
       <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Step 8: The new RC will then be issued to you, reflecting the vehicle's new registration details.</span></li>
   </ul></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


<section class="content-ui-section" style="padding: 55px 0; background: #0b132b; color: #cbd5e1; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07);">
